Application Deployment
(Deploy the given react application to a production ready state)

Application:

Clone the below mentioned repo and deploy the application(Run the application in port 80 [HTTP])

Repo URL: https://github.com/sriram-R-krishnan/devops-build

Docker:
 - Dockerize the application by creating a Dockerfile
 - Create a docker-compose file to use the above image

Bash Scripting:
write 2 scripts
 - build.sh - for building the docker images
 - deploy.sh - for deploying the image to server

Version Control:
- push to GitHub to dev branch (use dockerignore and gitignore files)
- Note: Use only CLI for related git commands

DockerHub:
- Create 2 repos "dev" and "prod" to push images
  "prod" repo must be private and "dev" repo can be public

Jenkins:
- Install and configure Jenkins build step as per needs to build,push and deploy the application.
- connect Jenkins to the GitHub repo with auto build trigger from both dev and master branch.
- If code pushed to dev branch , docker image must build and pushed to dev repo in docker hub.
- If dev merged to master , then docker image must be pushed to prod repo in docker hub

AWS:
Lanch t2.micro instance and deploy the create application.
Configure SG as below:
- whoever has ip address can access the application.
- login to server can should be made only from your ip

Monitoring:

Setup  a monitoring system to check the health status of application (open source).
sending notification only if the application goes down is highly appreciable.

Submission:

- GitHub repo URL,deployed site URL, docker images name must be added in the submission.

- Upload the screenshoots of below mentioned in GitHub repo:

   - Jenkins (login page, configuration setting, excecute step commands)
   - AWS (EC2- Console, SG config)
   - docker hub repo with image tags
   - Deployed site page 
   - Monitoring healthcheck status
